<article class="env-lemma" id="0H9Y">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H9Y">Lemma <span data-tag="0H9Y">15.23.5</span>.</a> Let $R \subset R'$ be an extension of domains. If $M$ is an $R$-module, then the rank of $M$ over $R$ is equal to the rank of $M \otimes _ R R'$ over $R'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because the dimension of a vector space is invariant under extension of ground field. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>